
     extern  unsigned int   My_mask;

     This is an integer bitmask that has a single bit set
for the user currently being processed.

     For example, if port 9 is the current user, then My_mask
would be 100 hex, or 512 decimal.  The binary representation is:

     3          2         1
     10987654321098765432109876543210
     --------------------------------
     00000000000000000000001000000000

     (This assumes a 32 bit integer.  A machine with 16 bit integers,
like the IBM PC, would have a maximum of 16 users in the bit mask.)
